scription>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134490381.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Heavy machinery has begun grading the former Vierling family farm in Minnesota for a new housing development. The Prior Lake City Council recently approved the plans for the 262-home neighborhood named Vierling Ridge. Pulte Homes aims to complete the main infrastructure by autumn, allowing construction to begin in winter. Various housing styles are planned, catering to different demographics and needs. The entire project is expected to be completed by 2032.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-minnesota-family-farm-has-been-sold-to-a-homebuilder-and-grading-has-already-begun-the-city-has-now-given-final-approval-to-turn-the-88-acre-property-into-a-262-home-community-by-2032/articleshow/134490381.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-minnesota-family-farm-has-been-sold-to-a-homebuilder-and-grading-has-already-begun-the-city-has-now-given-final-approval-to-turn-the-88-acre-property-into-a-262-home-community-by-2032/articleshow/134490381.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-25T23:46:46+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134490923,imgsize-1492805.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Trump-Xi bonhomie set to continue, leaders announce two more meetings]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134490297.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[US President Donald Trump and Chinese President Xi Jinping have agreed to meet in November and December. They will hold talks in China and at the G20 summit in Miami. These meetings aim to strengthen the relationship between the two largest economies. However, their recent discussions did not result in significant breakthroughs on various issues. Xi's visit included a state dinner and cultural exchanges during China's Mid-Autumn Festival.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/trump-xi-bonhomie-set-to-continue-leaders-announce-two-more-meetings/articleshow/134490297.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/trump-xi-bonhomie-set-to-continue-leaders-announce-two-more-meetings/articleshow/134490297.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-25T23:10:27+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Vijaya Srivastava</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134490402,imgsize-79164.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[At age 6, Grace opened a lemonade stand hoping to raise $10, seven summers later, she made $55,000]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134489553.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Grace Hendrian and her sister June initiated their Lemon-Aid Stand for Good in 2019 to support charity. They aimed to raise $10 but ultimately collected $55,000 for The Salvation Army. Their project encouraged community participation, leading to 14 stands operating by 2026. The sisters received recognition for their volunteer efforts as they also contributed to local families in need. Their fundraising initiative concluded in 2026, marking its final season.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/at-age-6-grace-hendrian-opened-a-lemonade-stand-hoping-to-raise-10-for-the-salvation-army-seven-summers-later-she-and-sister-june-closed-the-project-after-turning-that-tiny-goal-into-about-55000/articleshow/134489553.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/at-age-6-grace-hendrian-opened-a-lemonade-stand-hoping-to-raise-10-for-the-salvation-army-seven-summers-later-she-and-sister-june-closed-the-project-after-turning-that-tiny-goal-into-about-55000/articleshow/134489553.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-25T23:05:02+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134490336,imgsize-1088465.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA['Pure shock': Attorney Mariah Medina breaks silence as Internet debates over her sleeveless dress criticized by a Texas judge]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134490009.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/pure-shock-attorney-mariah-medina-breaks-silence-as-internet-debates-over-her-sleeveless-dress-criticized-by-a-texas-judge/articleshow/134490009.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/pure-shock-attorney-mariah-medina-breaks-silence-as-internet-debates-over-her-sleeveless-dress-criticized-by-a-texas-judge/articleshow/134490009.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-25T22:45:40+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134490047,imgsize-56510.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Trump embraces Xi as peer, alarms partners and critics]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134489947.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/trump-embraces-xi-as-peer-alarms-partners-and-critics/articleshow/134489947.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/trump-embraces-xi-as-peer-alarms-partners-and-critics/articleshow/134489947.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-25T22:42:37+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Chidanand Rajghatta</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134489999,imgsize-74178.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[170 volunteers remove 43,000 pounds of trash from San Antonio dumping site after years of complaints]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134489475.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Around 170 volunteers have removed 43,000 pounds of trash from a long-standing dumping site outside Converse in Bexar County. The property had previously been used as an encampment and had drawn years of complaints. The county initially received a $100,000 cleanup estimate before River Aid San Antonio organized volunteer efforts. A final cleanup is planned for November 7.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/around-170-volunteers-remove-43000-pounds-of-trash-from-san-antonio-dumping-site-after-years-of-complaints-property-was-a-homeless-encampment-and-had-a-100000-cleanup-estimate/articleshow/134489475.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/around-170-volunteers-remove-43000-pounds-of-trash-from-san-antonio-dumping-site-after-years-of-complaints-property-was-a-homeless-encampment-and-had-a-100000-cleanup-estimate/articleshow/134489475.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-25T22:11:10+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134489529,imgsize-129786.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[UK PM Andy Burnham rules out early general polls, says ‘no election anytime soon’]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134489002.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/uk/uk-pm-andy-burnham-rules-out-early-general-polls-says-no-election-anytime-soon/articleshow/134489002.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/uk/uk-pm-andy-burnham-rules-out-early-general-polls-says-no-election-anytime-soon/articleshow/134489002.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-25T22:22:23+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Gokul Ankari</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134489704,imgsize-40806.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Pakistan goes bananas over giant gorillas dancing to Bollywood songs]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134488913.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[In Lahore, a vibrant new trend has emerged where massive gorillas are stealing the spotlight at weddings and celebrations. The concept, launched by Shayen Zahoor after receiving a gorilla costume in April, quickly captured attention on Instagram, amassing over a million views in just two days. This phenomenon led to a surge in event bookings, making these giant gorillas a delightful and unmistakable presence at gatherings across Pakistan.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/pakistan/pakistan-goes-bananas-over-giant-gorillas-dancing-to-bollywood-songs/articleshow/134488913.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/pakistan/pakistan-goes-bananas-over-giant-gorillas-dancing-to-bollywood-songs/articleshow/134488913.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-25T21:50:49+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Pranjal Pandey</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134489343,imgsize-48998.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[A Seattle shipbuilder sold his company for $3.5 million in 1906 and built an Orcas Island estate]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134487652.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Robert Moran established a thriving shipbuilding enterprise before shifting his focus to cultivate a serene habitat on Orcas Island. Upon receiving a terminal diagnosis, he chose to embrace the beauty of nature and safeguard the area. He generously donated land for what would become Moran State Park, a gift that would enhance public enjoyment, especially during the Great Depression. His legacy persists in fostering community engagement and conserving the environment.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-seattle-shipbuilder-sold-his-company-for-a-reported-3-5-million-in-1906-and-built-an-orcas-island-estate-15-years-later-he-donated-more-than-2700-acres-to-washington-to-create-moran-state-park/articleshow/134487652.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-seattle-shipbuilder-sold-his-company-for-a-reported-3-5-million-in-1906-and-built-an-orcas-island-estate-15-years-later-he-donated-more-than-2700-acres-to-washington-to-create-moran-state-park/articleshow/134487652.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-25T22:03:55+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134489482,imgsize-897243.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Singapore welcomes Southeast Asia’s first okapi calf: Why this rare ‘forest giraffe’ is so unusual]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134489107.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/singapore-welcomes-southeast-asias-first-okapi-calf-why-this-rare-forest-giraffe-is-so-unusual/articleshow/134489107.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA